\"fn\">j</span>)</span> <span class=\"fn\">⋯</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"On a variable generator, the intended generator image is the corresponding\nobservable unit:\n$$\n  \\rho_0(x_j) = \\operatorname{obs}_j.\n$$\nThis rewrite lemma is used to simplify the final representation on\n`SolutionGroup.var`.\n","docLink":"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.solutionGroupGeneratorImage_var","kind":"theorem","line":218,"name":"SolutionGroup.solutionGroupGeneratorImage_var","sourceLink":"https://github.com/sean-prz/lean/blob/d22cd063b437e364b0ca3c0e65dc5e07461a93fd/projects/LCS/LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.lean#L218-L232"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.solutionGroupGeneratorImage\"><span class=\"name\">SolutionGroup</span>.<span class=\"name\">solutionGroupGeneratorImage</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">S</span> : <a href=\"./LCS/Basic.html#LinearSystem\">LinearSystem</a>}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Defs.html#Fintype\">Fintype</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#DecidableEq\">DecidableEq</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">obs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">S</span>.<a href=\"./LCS/Basic.html#LinearSystem.layout\">layout</a></span>.<a href=\"./LCS/Basic.html#LCSLayout.s\">s</a></span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Defs.html#Matrix\">Matrix</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.html#Complex\">ℂ</a></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">obs_is_observable</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">j</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">S</span>.<a href=\"./LCS/Basic.html#LinearSystem.layout\">layout</a></span>.<a href=\"./LCS/Basic.html#LCSLayout.s\">s</a></span></span>), <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./LCS/Observable.html#IsObservable\">IsObservable</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">obs</span> <span class=\"fn\">j</span>)</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./LCS/SolutionGroup.html#SolutionGen\">SolutionGen</a> <span class=\"fn\">S</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Defs.html#Matrix\">Matrix</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.html#Complex\">ℂ</a>)</span><a href=\"./Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Units/Defs.html#Units\">ˣ</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The intended image of the solution-group generators in matrix units.\n\nThis is the generator-level assignment that all later constructors try to\ndescend through the quotient defining `SolutionGroup S`:\n\n```text\nvar j ↦ obs j\nJ     ↦ -I\n```\n","docLink":"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.solutionGroupGeneratorImage","kind":"def","line":201,"name":"SolutionGroup.solutionGroupGeneratorImage","sourceLink":"https://github.com/sean-prz/lean/blob/d22cd063b437e364b0ca3c0e65dc5e07461a93fd/projects/LCS/LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.lean#L201-L216"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.bipartiteAliceLift_noncommProd\"><span class=\"name\">SolutionGroup</span>.<span class=\"name\">bipartiteAliceLift_noncommProd</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Defs.html#Fintype\">Fintype</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#DecidableEq\">DecidableEq</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_2}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Finset/Defs.html#Finset\">Finset</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Defs.html#Matrix\">Matrix</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.html#Complex\">ℂ</a></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">comm</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(↑<span class=\"fn\">s</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./Mathlib/Logic/Pairwise.html#Set.Pairwise\">Pairwise</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">x</span> <span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Commute/Defs.html#Commute\">Commute</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span>)</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">y</span>)</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./LCS/Strategy/ObservableStrategy.html#bipartiteAliceLift\">bipartiteAliceLift</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">s</span>.<a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Finset/NoncommProd.html#Finset.noncommProd\">noncommProd</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">comm</span>)</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">s</span>.<a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Finset/NoncommProd.html#Finset.noncommProd\">noncommProd</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">(fun (<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./LCS/Strategy/ObservableStrategy.html#bipartiteAliceLift\">bipartiteAliceLift</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span>)</span></span>)</span> <span class=\"fn\">⋯</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Alice lift commutes with finite noncommutative products:\n$$\n  \\operatorname{AliceLift}\\!\\left(\\prod_{x \\in s} f_x\\right)\n    = \\prod_{x \\in s}\\operatorname{AliceLift}(f_x).\n$$\nThe product is written with `Finset.noncommProd`, so pairwise commutation fixes\nthe order ambiguity.  This is useful when the EPR/local-loss row product\n`Alice_Row_Prod` must be identified with the Alice lift of the concrete row\nobservable product.\n","docLink":"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.bipartiteAliceLift_noncommProd","kind":"theorem","line":151,"name":"SolutionGroup.bipartiteAliceLift_noncommProd","sourceLink":"https://github.com/sean-prz/lean/blob/d22cd063b437e364b0ca3c0e65dc5e07461a93fd/projects/LCS/LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.lean#L151-L173"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.negOneMatrixUnit_sq\"><span class=\"name\">SolutionGroup</span>.<span class=\"name\">negOneMatrixUnit_sq</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Defs.html#Fintype\">Fintype</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#DecidableEq\">DecidableEq</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.negOneMatrixUnit\">negOneMatrixUnit</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HPow.hPow\">^</a> <span class=\"fn\">2</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The unit representing $J$ squares to $1$:\n$$\n  (-I)^2 = I.\n$$\nThis is the representation-side proof of the distinguished involution relator\n$J^2 = 1$.\n","docLink":"./LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.html#SolutionGroup.negOneMatrixUnit_sq","kind":"theorem","line":140,"name":"SolutionGroup.negOneMatrixUnit_sq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/sean-prz/lean/blob/d22cd063b437e364b0ca3c0e65dc5e07461a93fd/projects/LCS/LCS/SolutionGroup/Representation.lean#L140-L149"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=